no-poles:
&nbsp; 

 &nbsp; 
 Description 
 Tired of seeing 1 block wide stacks of blocks in your world? This mod prevents them. No more stone, dirt, wood or other single-block columns. Your players will have to put some thought into their constructs, like a staircase, or a pole with a ladder. 
 &nbsp; 
 When a player right-clicks the top of a column whose four sides are open for the configured height (10 blocks by default), the column is removed down to the ground and its blocks drop as items. Unbreakable blocks such as bedrock are left in place, and removal never goes below the bottom of the world. 
 &nbsp; 
 This doesn't stop all kinds of ugly, just that one type of ugly with the single stack of blocks reaching high above the ground. 
 &nbsp; 
 Whitelist 
 A whitelist lets you allow nerdpoling with specific blocks. By default it contains Minecraft sand, red sand, gravel and the NotEnoughScaffol

